{
  "version": "0.3.3",
  "notes": "Fix a hard crash when handling BLE commands (e.g. tapping Refresh in the app killed the Pico's USB-serial link entirely). handle_command()/update_status() do I2C reads, JSON serialization, and gatts_write/notify -- calling all of that directly inside the BLE IRQ callback (_IRQ_GATTS_WRITE / _IRQ_CENTRAL_CONNECT) can corrupt the BLE stack's internal state, per MicroPython's own documented IRQ constraints. Now deferred via micropython.schedule() to run safely outside the IRQ context. Also includes prior fixes: BLE advertising overflow (34 > 31 byte limit), WiFi-off before BLE with a settle delay, and non-fatal gap_advertise error handling.",
